.TH CTBREC-MERGE-REMOTE 1 "2026-10-01" "ctbrec-merge-remote" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ctbrec-merge-remote \- run ctbrec-merge on the Proxmox server over ssh
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ctbrec-merge-remote
[\fIOPTIONS\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ctbrec-merge-remote
is a thin local wrapper that runs
.BR ctbrec-merge (1)
on the Proxmox server.
.P
It connects with
.BR ssh (1)
(non-interactive, no TTY, with the host's
.B RemoteCommand
disabled) and executes
.B /usr/local/bin/ctbrec-merge
with
.B \-\-dir /mnt/pve/Data_Storage/ctbrec
plus any arguments given to the wrapper. All scanning, probing, and merging
happen on the server; nothing is copied to the local machine. The remote
interpreter is run with
.B PYTHONUNBUFFERED\=1
so that, despite ssh having no TTY, progress lines stream back live instead of
arriving in buffered blocks. Standard output and standard error are streamed
back, and the remote exit status is returned as the wrapper's exit status.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-detach
Run the remote job in a detached session on the server while still streaming
its output here. The command runs under
.BR setsid (1)
with its output written to a log file; the wrapper follows that file with
.BR tail (1)
so updates appear live on the terminal exactly as in the normal mode. Because
the job is in its own session, closing the terminal or losing the ssh connection
does not stop it: the streamed view ends, but the merge keeps running on the
server. The remote exit status is still returned when the job finishes while
connected, and the log file path is printed so the run can be inspected later.
.TP
.B \-\-ignore\-storage\-limit
Run even when the target filesystem is below the
.B \-\-min\-free\-pct
threshold (default 3.81%). The wrapper translates this flag into
.B \-\-min\-free\-pct 0
for the remote
.BR ctbrec-merge (1),
bypassing the coarse free\-space gate. The per\-group check that still requires
enough room for a group's output plus a
.B 1 GB
margin remains in force, so the run stops naturally once the drive is nearly
full. If
.B \-\-min\-free\-pct
is also given on the command line, this flag wins.
.P
All other options are forwarded verbatim to
.BR ctbrec-merge (1);
see that page for the full list. The most useful are
.BR \-\-dry\-run ,
.BR \-\-keep ,
and
.BR \-\-verify .
.P
Unlike
.BR \-\-detach ,
without it a disconnect sends
.B SIGHUP
to the remote process group and the job is terminated.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CTBREC_MERGE_SERVER
Ssh host (or alias from
.BR ssh_config (5))
to run on. Defaults to
.BR proxmox .
.TP
.B CTBREC_MERGE_BIN
Path to the remote executable. Defaults to
.BR /usr/local/bin/ctbrec-merge .
.TP
.B CTBREC_MERGE_DIR
Remote recordings root passed as
.BR \-\-dir .
Defaults to
.BR /mnt/pve/Data_Storage/ctbrec .
.SH EXAMPLES
Preview the merge plan on the server:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-merge-remote \-\-dry\-run
.EE
.P
Merge on the server, verifying each output:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-merge-remote \-\-verify
.EE
.P
Merge on the server so the job survives closing the terminal:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-merge-remote \-\-detach \-\-verify
.EE
.P
Merge on a drive that is below the 3.81% free threshold:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-merge-remote \-\-ignore\-storage\-limit \-\-verify
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status of the remote
.BR ctbrec-merge (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ctbrec-merge (1),
.BR ssh (1),
.BR setsid (1),
.BR tail (1)
